  <section><h2>What Redax does</h2><p>Redax detects configured entities, applies a versioned policy, and returns transformed text. Structured regex detection is the stable lightweight path; the pinned local GLiNER2 path adds contextual entities when its model is available. The browser demo is intentionally illustrative and does not claim server-side parity.</p></section>
  <section class="rdx-docs-callout rdx-docs-warning"><b>Read the boundary before sending real data.</b><p>Detection is configured coverage, not proof of absence. Review the threat model, data flow, failure modes, policy pass-through behavior, provider logging, infrastructure access, and retention before production use.</p><a href="/redax/docs/security">Read the security boundary →</a></section>
